open cuts a file with data past its last committed record without looking
at the other hint-less files, so damage that leaves two such files, a
zeroed first header beside a torn newest file, is cut as two torn tails.
Guarded-by: "DB recovery: a hint-less file's tail is truncated only in the newest file"

